{"name":"Positive Energy","hex":"#e1e2cf","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"positive","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Included, present, characterized by affirmation.","Formally laid down. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thing capable of being affirmed; something real or actual.","A favourable point or characteristic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/positive"},{"term":"energy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The impetus behind all motion and all activity.","The capacity to do work."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/energy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Positive energy theorem","blocks":[{"text":"The positive energy theorem refers to a collection of foundational results in general relativity and differential geometry. Its standard form, broadly speaking, asserts that the gravitational energy of an isolated system is nonnegative, and can only be zero when the system has no gravitating objects. Although these statements are often thought of as being primarily physical in nature, they can be formalized as mathematical theorems which can be proven using techniques of differential geometry, partial differential equations, and geometric measure theory."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Positive_energy_theorem"},{"title":"Positive energy (China)","blocks":[{"text":"Positive energy is an expression commonly used in Chinese Communist Party political discourse, referring to the need for uplifting messages as opposed to critical or negative ones. First popularized in 2012 by Xi Jinping at the 18th National Congress of the Chinese Communist Party, it has since become central to other areas of CCP and government policy. Chinese internet censors typically remove content that is not deemed to promote positive energy."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Positive_energy_(China)"},{"title":"Energy","blocks":[{"text":"Energy is the quantitative property that is transferred to a body or to a physical system, recognizable in the capacity to do work and in the form of heat and light. Energy is a conserved quantity – the law of conservation of energy states that the total energy of an isolated system remains constant, although it can be converted in form. The unit of measurement for energy in the International System of Units (SI) is the joule (J)."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/330px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Energy"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/500px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/1280px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Plasma_globe_60th.jpg/500px-Plasma_globe_60th.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlasma_globe_60th.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg/500px-Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg/1280px-Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg/500px-Lightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In a typical lightning strike, 500 megajoules of electric potential energy is converted into the same amount of energy in other forms, mostly light energy, sound energy, and thermal energy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALightning_over_Oradea_Romania_zoom.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Hot_metalwork.jpg/500px-Hot_metalwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Hot_metalwork.jpg/1280px-Hot_metalwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a9/Hot_metalwork.jpg/500px-Hot_metalwork.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thermal energy is energy of microscopic constituents of matter, which may include both kinetic and potential energy.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHot_metalwork.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Portrait_of_Thomas_Young_with_printed_autograph.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Thomas_Young_with_printed_autograph.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Portrait_of_Thomas_Young_with_printed_autograph.jpg/1280px-Portrait_of_Thomas_Young_with_printed_autograph.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Portrait_of_Thomas_Young_with_printed_autograph.jpg/500px-Portrait_of_Thomas_Young_with_printed_autograph.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Thomas Young, the first person to use the term \"energy\" in the modern sense","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APortrait_of_Thomas_Young_with_printed_autograph.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Joule%27s_Apparatus_%28Harper%27s_Scan%29.pn